  "description": "Search 19 additional tools that are loaded on demand. Send one keyword query per capability you need; returns matching tool names and descriptions. Then `tool_describe` loads schemas and `tool_call` invokes. Tools already in your tool list need no search. Searches also cover the user's connected app accounts, whose tools are hosted and so never listed here (results named `connectors__<app>__<tool>`); `manage_connections` checks or connects an account.\n\nEvery tool listed below exists: never call it unavailable, and go straight to `tool_describe` when you see the exact name.\n\nDeferred tool catalog (call schemas via `tool_describe`, invoke via `tool_call`):\n- browser_vault: Fill saved logins, 2FA codes, cards and addresses on the CURRENT browser page.\n- manage_catalog: Find and install Hermes catalog plugins and hub skills for the user.\n- computer_use: Drive the desktop via cua-driver: screenshots, mouse, keyboard, scroll, drag.\n- cronjob_manage: Schedule recurring or one-off agent tasks (cron jobs): create, list, edit, run.\n- image_generate: Generate or edit images (with reference images) using the configured model.\n- desktop_project: Create or switch desktop Projects (named workspaces).\n- session_search: Search or read past Hermes conversations (FTS5), or scroll inside one.\n- process_manage: Poll, wait on, send input to, or kill terminal(background=true) processes.\n- todo_list: Track a task list for multi-step work (3+ steps).\ndesktop_ui tools (10):\n- annotate_preview: Highlight preview-pane elements with lasting marks (drive_preview's fade).\n- close_terminal: Hide a background process's desktop terminal tab; the process keeps running.\n- desktop_preview: Open, close, or read the preview pane beside the chat.\n- drive_preview: Use the desktop preview-pane page: log in, fill forms, click through flows.\n- focus_pane: Show a desktop pane: chat, files, terminal, review (git diff) or sessions.\n- gui_tour: Run a guided desktop GUI tour: dim the screen, highlight elements, add popovers.\n- read_terminal: Read the in-app terminal pane beside this chat.\n- read_window_below: Identify the app window behind the Hermes desktop window (what the user is in).\n- set_theme: Change how the Hermes desktop app looks: accent colour, light/dark mode, layout.\n- show_tip: Point at one desktop UI element with a small arrow bubble (no dimming or tour).",
